{
  "statement": "Whether a message is a question about what they have put in or something to keep is decided on the text alone, before anything is read. A note with a question mark is still a note, anything ambiguous files, and a message that both asks and dumps is a dump.",
  "why": "An unwanted row is archived in a second; a note treated as a question is lost. So the call fails towards filing, and it is made before retrieval so the same sentence lands the same way whatever the corpus holds.",
